---
import { Image } from "astro:assets"
import SectionTitle from "~/components/security/SectionTitle.astro"
import BrowserFrame from "./BrowserFrame.astro"
import { GUIDE_HREF } from "./links"
import briefFront from "../assets/assistant-brief-front.webp"
---

<section class="overview">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="intro-row">
            <div class="intro">
                <SectionTitle title="What it does" />
                <p>
                    The Migration Assistant runs the assessment for moving off
                    VMware vRA and vRO to Kestra. It covers the workflow half of{" "}
                    <a href={`${GUIDE_HREF}#section-3`}
                        >Stage 1 of the vRA migration guide</a
                    >:
                    it reads your vRO package and vRA export, works out what's
                    in the estate, and writes a brief you open in a browser.
                </p>
            </div>
            <div class="covers">
                <h3>The brief covers</h3>
                <ul class="list-unstyled">
                    <li>
                        <strong
                            >What each workflow does and what starts it</strong
                        >
                        <span
                            >Including the catalog items, cloud templates and
                            event subscriptions in the vRA export.</span
                        >
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Which systems each workflow touches</strong>
                        <span
                            >And whether a <a href="/plugins">Kestra plugin</a> already
                            exists for each one.</span
                        >
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>A recommendation for each workflow</strong>
                        <span
                            >Retire, merge into another, treat as a wrapper,
                            convert, or rebuild, with the reason next to it.</span
                        >
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>A migration plan in waves</strong>
                        <span
                            >Ordered by risk and dependency, with what each wave
                            needs before it starts.</span
                        >
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>

        <figure>
            <div class="stage">
                <BrowserFrame path="kestra-assessment / index.html">
                    <Image
                        src={briefFront}
                        alt="The front page of the migration brief for the load balancer example: the next step, what's in the estate, and the recommendation to convert, with 50 of 59 elements on a path to Kestra before the open questions are answered."
                        widths={[640, 960, 1280, 1848]}
                        sizes="(min-width: 1416px) 924px, 70vw"
                    />
                </BrowserFrame>
            </div>
            <figcaption>
                <p>
                    <strong>The front page leads with what to do next.</strong> The
                    tool stops at the plan: converting the workflows, testing them
                    and verifying each wave before cutover is work Kestra does with
                    you, starting from the brief.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Still deciding? Read the <a href={GUIDE_HREF}
                        >introduction to the guide</a
                    > or try the <a href="/resources/migration/vra/payback"
                        >payback calculator</a
                    >.
                </p>
            </figcaption>
        </figure>
    </div>
</section>

<style lang="scss">
    @use "/src/components/vra-migration-guide/shared" as *;

    .overview {
        @include assistant-section(var(--ks-background-body));
    }

    .container {
        @include guide-container;
    }

    a {
        color: var(--ks-content-link);
        text-decoration: underline;
        text-underline-offset: 3px;
    }

    .intro a {
        color: inherit;
    }

    strong {
        font-weight: 600;
    }

    .intro-row {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
        gap: 2rem;

        @include media-breakpoint-up(xl) {
            grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 521px) minmax(0, 1fr);
        }
    }

    .intro p {
        margin: 1rem 0 0;
        font-size: $font-size-lg;
        line-height: 1.75rem;
    }

    .covers {
        h3 {
            margin: 0 0 1rem;
            font-size: $font-size-lg;
            font-weight: 700;
            line-height: 1.75rem;
            color: var(--ks-content-link);
        }

        ul {
            display: grid;
            grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
            gap: 1rem;
            margin: 0;

            @include media-breakpoint-up(md) {
                grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
            }
        }

        li {
            display: flex;
            flex-direction: column;
            gap: 0.25rem;
            @include calc-card;
            padding: 1rem;

            strong {
                font-size: $font-size-lg;
                line-height: 1.75rem;
            }

            span {
                font-size: $font-size-sm;
                line-height: 1.25rem;
                color: var(--ks-content-secondary);
            }
        }
    }

    figure {
        margin: 4rem 0 0;
    }

    .stage {
        aspect-ratio: 1320 / 675;
        overflow: hidden;
        padding: 3.52% 15% 0;
        border-radius: 1rem;
        background: linear-gradient(to bottom, #81bdd4 1%, #e8e8f9);

        @include media-breakpoint-down(md) {
            aspect-ratio: 4 / 3;
            padding-inline: 6%;
        }
    }

    figcaption {
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        gap: 1rem;
        margin-top: 1rem;
        padding-inline: 1.25rem;

        @include media-breakpoint-up(xl) {
            flex-direction: row;
            gap: 4rem;
        }

        p {
            flex: 1;
            margin: 0;
        }

        p + p {
            flex: 0 1 auto;
        }
    }
</style>
